            "execution_time_sec": 80.83085762799965,
            "final_response_preview": "\"Completed: /app/headless_terminal.py implemented.\\n\\nWhat I implemented\\n- HeadlessTerminal(BaseTerminal) in /app/headless_terminal.py\\n- Launches an interactive bash (/bin/bash -i) on a PTY so startup files are sourced\\n- Background reader thread collects terminal output into an internal buffer\\n- send_keystrokes(keystrokes: str, wait_sec: float = 0.0) writes raw bytes (supports control chars like \\\\x03 for Ctrl-C) and optionally waits\\n- read(drain: bool = True) returns accumulated output (drainable); peek() returns buffer without clearing\\n- close() terminates the shell and cleans up fds; supports context-manager usage\\n- No extra system packages required (uses stdlib: pty, os, subprocess, select, threading)\\n\\nVerification performed\\n- Ran a runtime test in the container: started HeadlessTerminal, executed `echo hello_terminal`, and sent Ctrl-C during `sleep 3`. The test returned PASS; outputs contained the expected echo and Ctrl-C (^C).\\n\\nFile location\\n- /app/headless_terminal."
